#!/bin/sh
#
# Refuses a commit that stages NEW files, unless adding them was deliberate.
#
# Why additions and not, say, a file count. Two commits swept another session's work into
# this repository — c861bac on 26 August (.fn-dump/ and four scripts/eval/_*.ts) and ffe217c
# on 5 September (scripts/tmp-nan.ts). Both came from `git add -A`. Measured afterwards:
# every swept path was status A, an addition of a previously untracked file, while ordinary
# commits here are M. And a size threshold would have missed the second one — it was six
# files, an ordinary size.
#
# So the dangerous surface is precisely the untracked one: `git add -A` claims the whole
# tree, which is false in a repository where parallel sessions and Lovable write at the same
# time. Modifying a tracked file is something you did; adding an untracked one may be
# something someone else did.
#
# The guard fires only when files are added, which is roughly one commit in three, and turns
# adding into a deliberate act rather than a side effect.
#
#   COMPASS_AJOUTS=1 git commit ...     # yes, these new files are mine
#
# What this does NOT catch, and it matters: a *modification* to a tracked file that another
# session made. Nothing here can tell that apart from one of yours — git records what changed,
# never who was working. Staging by name rather than by sweep remains the rule; this only
# removes the accident that has actually happened twice.

ajouts=$(git diff --cached --name-only --diff-filter=A)

[ -z "$ajouts" ] && exit 0

if [ -n "$COMPASS_AJOUTS" ]; then
  exit 0
fi

n=$(printf '%s\n' "$ajouts" | grep -c .)

cat >&2 <<AVERTISSEMENT

  Ce commit ajoute $n fichier(s) jusque-la non suivi(s) :

$(printf '%s\n' "$ajouts" | sed 's/^/      /')

  Deux commits ont deja emporte le travail d'une session parallele de cette facon
  (c861bac le 26 aout, ffe217c le 5 septembre), et les deux venaient d'un git add -A.

  Si ces fichiers sont bien les tiens :

      COMPASS_AJOUTS=1 git commit ...

  Sinon : git restore --staged <chemin> pour ceux qui ne le sont pas.

AVERTISSEMENT

exit 1
